What it does
The opening graph focuses on stocks purchased by at least two different politicians, making shared holdings easier to see without treating the display filter as a data-quality rule.
Users can:

search politicians, stocks, committees, and subcommittees;
inspect the original PTR purchase records behind a stock;
open committee and subcommittee drawers;
see members with matched purchases alongside members with no accepted purchase found;
export institution-level CSV summaries;
copy links to selected drill-down states;
compare the graph with a broader House coverage panel.
